From 6806e8a7a3cee116a1a10233221a3e3bed51bf3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pugant <pugant@localhost>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:06:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/19] w6a3: gauge timing in e2e tests

run_gauge() in test-park-mirror measures the W6 card's wall metrics on the
same CPU-only e2e paths, printing W6-GAUGE:-prefixed lines for grepping:
(a) restore-from-disk single cold read (W6-5) and the old two-pass restore
reconstructed from its building blocks (whole-file CRC verify pass + file-IO
load pass, both after DONTNEED), (b) restore-from-mirror (W6-8), (c) mirror
capture overhead (e2e save ON vs OFF), (d) save in-stream CRC (W6-7) vs the
old write+sync+cold-re-read sequence. Median of 3 per metric, steady_clock.
The gauge model is 8x1024 with f16 KV (~32 KiB/token): a 4096-token state
lands at ~128 MiB of payload - the scale the live host gauge exercised. The
gauge dir defaults to /var/tmp because /tmp is tmpfs on the target host
(a RAM filesystem would turn every cold read into a memcpy); override with
W6A3_GAUGE_DIR. Save the run output as logs/wave6/w6a3-gauge-test.log.

Test-only change: no production code touched.

Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai
